[]($section.id('about'))
sqlz has no tagged release yet. This log records notable milestones on
`main`; the full history is in the
[commit log](https://github.com/westack-it/sqlz/commits/main).

# [Zig 0.17]($section.id('zig-0.17').data('date','2026-11-08'))

- The toolchain and all dependencies moved to Zig 0.17.0.

# [Source manager and lexer]($section.id('source-and-lexer').data('date','2026-10-20'))

- A source manager handles BOMs, UTF-8 validation, scalar columns and LF/CRLF
  line endings for every diagnostic.
- A shared, dialect-aware SQL lexer with enforced token and nesting limits.
- Source trust boundaries: every input must resolve inside the project root,
  and symlinked directories inside a root fail the check.
- Each project declares its own runtime backends with
  `ProjectOptions.runtime`.

>[]($block.attrs('warning'))
>`addProject` now panics at configure time when `.runtime` names a backend the
>sqlz dependency was configured without.

# [Diagnostics]($section.id('diagnostics').data('date','2026-09-19'))

- PostgreSQL syntax errors, migration graph errors, catalog and semantic
  errors are reported with source spans and excerpts.
- Diagnostics are also available as versioned JSON.
- PostgreSQL server versions are enforced at connect time.

# [PostgreSQL]($section.id('postgres').data('date','2026-09-18'))

- Offline PostgreSQL migration replay, enum, domain and array checking.
- A pg.zig runtime adapter with pools, one-dimensional arrays and a live
  conformance matrix for PostgreSQL 15–18.
- Backend-specific query variants and lazy runtime backend selection.
- An experimental `zig build sqlz -- bootstrap postgres` command that copies a
  SQLite database into PostgreSQL.

# [Checked queries on SQLite]($section.id('sqlite').data('date','2026-09-17'))

- The checker, binding generator and SQLite runtime: all four cardinalities,
  borrowed and owned rows, transactions, pools and enum codecs.
- Queries declared in Zig with `sqlz.Query` are checked, including their
  `.params` and `.row` structs.
